    "hints": [
      {
        "x": 2,
        "y": 2,
        "r": 2,
        "icon": "⛏️",
        "title": "THE DEEP ELEMENT RUN",
        "text": "One colossal cavern. <strong>All 94 elements found in nature</strong>. Each hall holds one family of the periodic table. <strong>Finish a family and the clock gains time</strong>; the doors between the halls ask about the family you have just met, so read the signs. Good luck, miner!"
      },
      {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 3,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🌱",
        "title": "NONMETALS",
        "text": "The elements of <strong>life itself</strong> - carbon, oxygen, nitrogen… You are mostly made of this hall. The halogens and noble gases are nonmetals too, with halls of their own - so this family is called the <em>other nonmetals</em>."
      },
      {
        "x": 42,
        "y": 3,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🧪",
        "title": "HALOGENS",
        "text": "Salt-formers - fiercely reactive, and <em>toxic as gases</em>. Those barrels? <strong>Walk east and shove them</strong> - each drops down a chute, and the blast cracks the ice vault holding a halogen."
      },
      {
        "x": 69,
        "y": 6,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "👑",
        "title": "NOBLE GASES",
        "text": "The loners of chemistry: they react with almost <strong>nothing</strong>. Fittingly, someone locked them away. One key lies here. <strong>The other two were dropped in the flooded hall to the west</strong>."
      },
      {
        "x": 43,
        "y": 9,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "💥",
        "title": "ALKALI METALS",
        "text": "Soft, shiny metals that all <strong>react with water</strong> - some of them violently. Naturally, this hall is flooded. Keep your head up and watch for swimmers."
      },
      {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 9,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🦴",
        "title": "ALKALINE EARTH METALS",
        "text": "Calcium in your bones, magnesium in your greens - the sturdy builders of the mineral world."
      },
      {
        "x": 2,
        "y": 14,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "💻",
        "title": "METALLOIDS",
        "text": "Half metal, half not - silicon is at the heart of nearly every computer chip. Their crystals hide behind <strong>glacial ice</strong>: dynamite time (press 1, then RUN)."
      },
      {
        "x": 26,
        "y": 16,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🥫",
        "title": "OTHER METALS",
        "text": "The metals to the right of the transition metals - aluminium cans, tin solder, lead pipes. Most are soft and melt easily: gallium would melt in your hand. Mind the old rail carts."
      },
      {
        "x": 47,
        "y": 22,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "⚙️",
        "title": "TRANSITION METALS",
        "text": "The <strong>backbone of civilisation</strong> - iron, copper, gold, titanium. They lie <strong>in order of atomic number</strong>: east along the top gallery from scandium, back west along the middle one, east again along the bottom to mercury. The machines still run. Cross with care."
      },
      {
        "x": 5,
        "y": 31,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🧲",
        "title": "LANTHANIDES",
        "text": "Fifteen of the seventeen <em>rare earths</em> - magnets in your headphones, colours in your screen. Not actually rare, just devilishly hard to separate. It's dark down here - lamps on (press 2), and tread quietly."
      },
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 35,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "☢️",
        "title": "ACTINIDES",
        "text": "Radioactive heavyweights - uranium, thorium, plutonium. Real uranium ore does not glow - the <strong>glowing</strong> veins down here are lava. Never dig glowing ground."
      },
      {
        "x": 57,
        "y": 35,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🔬",
        "title": "THE SYNTHETICS VAULT",
        "text": "Beyond this door lie elements <strong>no mine has ever held</strong> - people made them in reactors and laboratories, the heaviest only a few atoms at a time. Answer the question to enter; hunt them with the Geiger Counter (press 3). Pure bonus - the core does not wait for them."
      },
      {
        "x": 45,
        "y": 41,
        "r": 1,
        "icon": "🌍",
        "title": "THE CORE",
        "text": "You hold every element found in nature. <strong>Step into the core and finish your run</strong> - but tread lightly: <em>something guards it</em>."
      },
      {
        "x": 9,
        "y": 7,
        "r": 3,
        "icon": "⛑️",
        "title": "REFUGE CHAMBER",
        "text": "Real mines keep sealed <strong>refuge chambers</strong> stocked with air and water. Step inside to <strong>save your progress</strong> - if the deep claims you, you respawn here. There are three on the way down."
      }
    ],
